; MM-RGN-3, the escape rule, at a STORE (docs/memory-model-v2-design.md
; §2.3; stage S3 of §4). A value may be stored only into a place its
; own region outlives. Four functions, each a different door:
;
;   1  `putField`   `(set c.s x)`: `@s` into a `@r` cell. Two named
;                   regions are UNORDERED, so refused - at the store.
;   2  `putSame`    the same store with both in `@r`: SILENT. This is
;                   the accepted half that keeps the refusals honest.
;   3  `putVec`     `(vecPush v x)`: the store is made by a CALLEE.
;                   `vecPush` names no region, so the compiler reads
;                   its body (`rgnKnownCall`, typecheck.ax) and finds
;                   TWO flows into its first parameter, each a row:
;                   its second parameter (`x`, `@s`, refused as in 1),
;                   and the buffer it ALLOCATES when it grows - a
;                   value in this function's own region, which is
;                   its caller's current region and does not outlive
;                   `@r`. That second row is the honest one: under
;                   this stage nothing can grow a container that lives
;                   in a named region, because allocating INTO a named
;                   region is stage S4's work. The rows name `vecPush`
;                   and its parameter.
;   4  `putFresh`   `(vecPush v (strConcat x "!"))`: the growth row
;                   again, and the fresh string through `vecPush`'s
;                   second parameter - both "a value allocated in this
;                   function's own region", by two doors.
;
; Every refusal carries the STORE's span, not the declaration's: the
; fix is where the store is.
;
; ABLATION: `scripts/check-region-escape.sh` builds a compiler whose
; `rgnCheckAll` answers 0, requires this file to be ACCEPTED by it,
; and runs the program that compiler lets through - `tests/region/
; escape-store.ax` - which reclaims the region past the stored value
; and reads it back.
(import IO)

(import Vec)

(import Str)

(struct Cell
  (mut s : String))

(:: putField (-> (Cell @r) (String @s) Int))

(fn (putField c x)
  {
    (set c.s x)
    0
  }
)

(:: putSame (-> (Cell @r) (String @r) Int))

(fn (putSame c x)
  {
    (set c.s x)
    0
  }
)

(:: putVec (-> (Vec String @r) (String @s) Int))

(fn (putVec v x)
  {
    (vecPush v x)
    0
  }
)

(:: putFresh (-> (Vec String @r) String Int))

(fn (putFresh v x)
  {
    (vecPush v (strConcat x "!"))
    0
  }
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
